{
  "form": "CCSI Online Direct Coil — DX",
  "version": "2026-07-04",
  "url_pattern": "https://coil.ccsi.ie/Coils/*",
  "framework": "jquery-server-rendered (ASP.NET MVC + Bootstrap; no virtual DOM)",
  "_note": "Phase 0 captured live on coil.ccsi.ie/Coils/Edit (CDXC-1, 2026-06-28); Phase 2.0 added the 12 multi-header keys (I2/S2/O2/R2/HD2/ZD2, I3/S3/O3/R3/HD3/ZD3) captured live 2026-07-04 on the same editor from a 3-header DX coil (3025 Bauducco, /Coils/Edit/8182979). CCSI's internal field ids differ from CoilForge's drawing-param labels for 8 of 13 base (I→HS, S→VS, O→HR, R→VR, RF→EF, HF→FF, SL→CS, ZD→DX_ZD); multi-header ids follow a `DX_<stem><N>` pattern (I2→DX_HS2, S2→DX_VS2, O2→DX_HR2, R2→DX_VR2, HD2→DX_HD2, ZD2→DX_ZD2, …3 for header 3), all editable (not readonly). Each `selectors` list tries the real CCSI id first, then falls back to CoilForge's own mirror ([data-ccsi-key='<KEY>']) so the SAME map self-tests same-origin on localhost:8011. `ccsi_readonly:true` marks fields CCSI computes itself (RF/HF/CH observed readonly live 2026-07-04; base CD was captured readonly 2026-06-28 but showed editable in the 2026-07-04 DOM — left as-is pending confirmation, since skipping CD is the conservative direction) — the userscript skips these instead of overwriting. 4HD keys (I4…) are NOT added until captured live from a real 4-header coil (never invented).",
